{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794783083,"nonce":"heHOo5HfWid9AQ6tNZplzG2iD6w=","message":"Go from the user, 2026-11-15: proceed, as long as AIR does not lose data the direct compile affords. That settles decisions 1, 2 and 3 as recommended: one module interface in the air crate (ModuleInfo, widened), module-wide facts computed from AIR at load, and engines receiving optimized AIR with its facts (they ride on Function, so no pass or handoff strips them). The runtime-owned address provider stays a separate trait. Decisions 4 to 6 are still open.\n\nRule for every widening: a query gets a test that compiles the same Haxe both ways and requires nAIR and genhl to answer alike; where nAIR knows more than the bytecode can say, the extra is a method whose default is \"unknown\", so a bytecode module is unchanged.\n\nPhase 1, f6e61d2b: ModuleInfo::type_kind (a TypeKind for every type) and fun_sig (arguments and return type, bytecode or native). is_float, value_is_i32, value_is_small_uint and tree fusion's is_i32 and is_void are derived from type_kind. AshModule and NairModule implement both; ash_nair_hl/tests/module_info.rs checks agreement on three fixtures. The \u0026T forwarding impl now forwards every method; before, it dropped seven.\n\nNext phases, in order. 2: type_param (Ref, Packed), object layout and field hash, string and byte pools, float pool, and a target word size (the lane-size mismatch between the passes and the wasm emitter). 3: Cranelift's context holds the module interface, not a bytecode pointer, and matches TypeKind; then an nAIR numeric kernel runs on Cranelift with no bytecode. 4: the AIR provider takes a findex and asks the module for its AIR (the three lowering sites move into the bytecode implementation), and OSR and profile keys move from opcode positions to (findex, BlockId). 5: tree fusion becomes an overlay module with AIR-defined helpers, and generated.rs's serialization goes. 6: the walker, LLVM and wasm take the interface; then ash_nair_hl is deleted.","files":null}]}